        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "All three abort paths are fixed with guards scoped to the failing command: `cmp` in an `elif`, `grep -q` in an `if`, and `|| actual=\"<exit $?>\"` on the slugify capture. Each failure is recorded as one FAIL while the run continues and exits non-zero, and `set -e` was not disabled globally."
